WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.400
Need to

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:00.720
read an

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.440
older release

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.160
or recover

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.440
one earlier file.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.800
Git Checkout can do

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.280
both.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.320
The name covers

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.440
two different jobs,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.640
so first decide

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:08.960
what you

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.880
want to change.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.960
Selecting a branch

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:12.520
changes your

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.280
current development context.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.320
Selecting an older

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:15.960
commit lets

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.520
you inspect

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.160
that recorded

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.120
version directly.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.840
Git calls

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:19.880
that detached HEAD

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.360
your current

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.080
position points

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:21.320
to the

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:21.720
commit,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.120
rather than

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:22.880
a branch.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.600
Restoring one file is

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.320
different.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.520
Your branch stays

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:27.920
where it

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:28.320
is.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:28.880
You bring

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.920
back that file's

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.640
content.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:30.960
When the

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:31.600
source is

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.880
an earlier commit,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.000
that content also

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.200
enters the staging

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:35.720
area.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.960
Restoring can replace

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.000
local edits,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:39.560
so check

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:39.960
what you

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.600
would lose.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.920
Remember the distinction.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.640
Selecting changes your current

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.240
position.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.600
Restoring changes selected files.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.960
Same checkout name,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.040
different effects.
